rachel (docs): Small PR request: add a compact troubleshooting blurb for 429s/timeouts when large contexts or cold KV cache are suspected. Need two tiny snippets (py/js), backoff recommendation, and a migration note about trim helpers.

omar (eng-runtime): Keep it short: honor Retry-After if present; otherwise exponential backoff + full jitter, cap ~30s; after ~3 retries suggest a lighter/quantized model or surface a clear error. Note KV-cache cold starts can cause initial timeouts — suggest a warmup or one quick retry.

li (devex): JS snippet (AbortController + retry):```js
async function callWithRetry(url, opts = {}, maxRetries = 3) {
  for (let i = 0; i <= maxRetries; i++) {
    const ctrl = new AbortController();
    const t = setTimeout(() => ctrl.abort(), opts.timeout || 60000);
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url, { ...opts, signal: ctrl.signal });
      clearTimeout(t);
      if (res.status === 429) {
        const ra = res.headers.get('Retry-After');
        const wait = ra ? Number(ra) : Math.min(Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random(), 30);
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, wait * 1000));
        continue;
      }
      if (!res.ok) throw new Error('http error');
      return await res.json();
    } catch (e) {
      clearTimeout(t);
      if (e.name === 'AbortError' && i < maxRetries) {
        await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, (Math.pow(2, i) + Math.random()) * 1000));
        continue;
      }
      throw e;
    }
  }
}
```

li (devex): Python snippet (requests + jitter):```python
import time, random
import requests

def post_retry(url, payload, max_retries=3, timeout=60):
    for attempt in range(max_retries + 1):
        r = requests.post(url, json=payload, timeout=timeout)
        if r.status_code == 429:
            ra = r.headers.get('Retry-After')
            wait = int(ra) if ra and ra.isdigit() else min((2 ** attempt) + random.random(), 30)
            time.sleep(wait)
            continue
        r.raise_for_status()
        return r.json()
    raise RuntimeError('retries exhausted')
```

